Z||000000||gkozlov||05-05-2000||10:39 PM||||I am new to the forum. You guys and gals seem to really know your fiero's. I accidently shorted my hot wire on my stereo while installing my amp and sub. Now my speedometer does not work and my check engine light stays on. Any input on this would be great.||||reg||1
Z||000001||bad88||05-06-2000||12:22 AM||||Not knowing what year it is might be different for different years but according to the service manual the instrument panel and the radio are on the same fuse. It's a 10 amp fuse in the fuse box.  Does your radio still work? If so then its not the fuse unless you hotwired the radio to the fusebox.  Do you have cruise control?  Check that it comes off the same fuse also.  Looking at the diagram the ALDL (check engine light) connector does have a ground through the speedometer also so it looks like its probably the fuse but I'm not sure why the light would be on constantly without a ground.  It may be the radio causing the ground, check your connections again.  Hope that helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||gkozlov||05-06-2000||07:47 PM||||Thank it was a blown fuse which I checked but over-looked. I fell like a jack-@ss. Sorry and Thank you.||||reg||1
